---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import BikeshareDiagram from '../../components/diagrams/BikeshareDiagram.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Divvy demand forecasting"
  summary="A forecasting system for 200 Chicago bikeshare stations, 24 hours ahead — backtested on rolling origins, and measured for whether the forecast stays trustworthy once it is serving."
  metaDescription="Divvy demand forecasting by Quoc Nguyen: leakage-safe LightGBM backtesting, batch serving, monitoring, Docker, and CI."
  stack={[
    'Python',
    'Polars',
    'LightGBM',
    'MLflow',
    'Prefect',
    'FastAPI',
    'Evidently',
    'Docker',
    'GitHub Actions',
  ]}
  nextSteps={[
    'Replace historical weather replay with a live forecast-weather provider and monitor that train/serve gap.',
    'Deploy the API behind HTTPS and add a small station map for exploring the next 24 hours.',
    'Collect a complete unseen month before allowing the first champion/challenger promotion.',
  ]}
  draft={false}
>
  <Fragment slot="links">
    <a
      href="https://github.com/koshiroquoc/bikeshare-forecast"
      class="u-link inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-accent"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      repo ↗
    </a>
    <span class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-muted">
      local API · Docker Compose
    </span>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>
      Rebalancing a bikeshare network is a timing problem: operators need to know where
      demand will appear before a station becomes empty or full. A citywide total is not
      actionable, so the prediction target is demand for each station in each hour, one
      day ahead.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted">
      The hard part is not fitting a model. At a 24-hour horizon, recent trip counts are
      unavailable at prediction time; ordinary rolling features quietly leak them. The
      system therefore treats the station-hour grid, temporal cutoff, artifact version,
      and replay date as enforceable contracts rather than notebook conventions.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="diagram"><BikeshareDiagram /></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="diagram-caption">
    Fig. 02 — Trips and weather become leak-safe station-hour features. Versioned
    artifacts feed a batch prediction store; evaluation, drift, and promotion gates close
    the loop.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="evaluation">
    <div class="max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">
        Measured
      </span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
        MAE, RMSE, and MASE across four rolling-origin calendar months. Every model sees
        the same time cutoffs, and every target-derived feature uses information at least
        24 hours old.
      </p>
      <span class="mt-8 block font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">
        Eval design
      </span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        Each monthly window trains only on earlier rows, reserves the final training month
        for early stopping, and evaluates on the next unseen month. A leakage guard
        corrupts values that would be unavailable at serving time and verifies that the
        generated features do not change.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid max-w-[720px] grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-4">
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">1.101</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Final MAE
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">24.6%</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Vs. seasonal naive
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">51</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Tests in CI
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="data-scroll mt-12 max-w-[720px] overflow-x-auto"
      tabindex="0"
      role="region"
      aria-label="Four-month rolling-origin results. Scroll horizontally to see all metrics."
      data-scroll-label="Table · scroll horizontally →"
    >
      <table class="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left">
        <caption class="caption mb-4 text-left text-muted">
          Four-month rolling-origin results
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
              Predictor
            </th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
              MAE
            </th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
              RMSE
            </th>
            <th class="py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
              MASE
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-accent">LightGBM · Poisson</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">1.101</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">1.832</td>
            <td class="py-3">0.755</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Historical mean</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">1.198</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">2.267</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">0.820</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Seasonal naive</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">1.460</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">2.673</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">1.000</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">
        What failed → what was fixed
      </span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        An ordinary seven-day rolling mean would include trip counts from the previous
        1–23 hours—values unavailable for a 24-hour-ahead forecast. I replaced it with a
        same-hour daily window shifted by at least 24 hours, then added a corruption test
        that fails if future information changes an inference-time feature.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[60ch] border-l border-accent pl-6">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">
        Production evidence
      </span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        A seven-day historical replay completed 33,600 station-hour forecasts. Performance
        held at 1.410 MAE against a 1.706 alert threshold; the separate drift gate warned
        on changing inputs without mislabeling the model as failed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</ProjectLayout>
